 behind settling near the great  river anduin  this sets the stage for gollum's life  centuries later a distant hobby relative  of the stores and his discovery of the  one ring  as they move west many hobbits settle  into the area around debris  but it's not until the year 1601 of the  third age that the halflings finally  colonize the area that becomes known as  the shire  when settled the hobbits and their  descendants lived comfortably for  centuries  until the events of the war of the ring  force them to take their place  among the peoples of middle-earth as  they arrived in the shire the hobbits  become part of the dying kingdom of arno  a nation of men in the sister kingdom of  gondor some hobbits even claim to have  sent archers to help in one of arnold's  wars  however when the nation crumbles 500  years later the shayar hobbits declare  their independence which lasts for a  thousand years  as an independent people they begin to  elect a leader called athene to help  guide them  the first stain bucker of the marriage  ultimately founds the brandy burke  family  after a few hundred years one of his  descendants leads the brandy bugs from  the shire to colonize a neighbouring  region  that becomes known as buckland though  closely connected to the shire buckland  operates at his own independent entity  frodo's mother bramula brandy buck hails  from the small colony of hobbits fans of  the movie will recognize the name  buckleberry buckland's main village  it's mentioned in the fellowship of the  ring as frodo and his companions flee  from the black riders and cross the  river on the buckleberry ferry  while his mother grew up in buckland  frodo's paternal family traces its roots  completely to the shire his father's  family is much younger historically  speaking  the first bagen's balboa baggins shows  up not much more than a century before  bilbo was born the bagenses established  himself quickly but mostly concentrate  around the village of hobbiton they  in