ey spend more than a decade together  in an uneventful existence before  bilbo's fateful 111th birthday  frodo and bilbo share the same birthday  september 22nd  in fact in the fellowship of the ring  bilbo even states this as a condition  for why he feels frodo should come live  with him by living together they can  comfortably share their birthday parties  the bachelors have quite the annual to  do and go about hosting drone birthday  parties  when bilbo's 111th and frodo's 33rd  birthday fall on the same year they  decide to plan for a special celebration  111 years old is a particularly  respectable age for a hobbit to reach  and 33 is the point at which hobbits  consider their young ones have come of  age the event becomes a bigger deal than  anyone expected however  because unbeknownst to them bilbo has  decided to leave  my this would be a night to remember  bilbo chooses to abandon his comfortable  life again in the most dramatic fashion  he completely destroys his already shaky  reputation by using his magical ring  to vanish before the eyes of all the  party guests when the dust settles frodo  finds himself in possession of bilbo's  rink  and the unexpected new owner of bag end  where he continues to live his carefree  life for another 17 years  everything changes for frodo when he  turns 50 years old it's at this point  when gandalf the wizard arrives at his  doorstep  gandalf explains that the ring frodo has  held on to for so long  is actually the one ring forged  originally for sauron the dark lord  this revelation is the start of a grand  quest that leads the reluctant hobbit to  the village of brie  seeking council in rivendell through the  dark minds of moria  across the lands of gondor and  ultimately to the bleak land of mordor  the foreboding domain where the ring was  forged on his journey  frodo learns to overcome his fears and  accept his calling as a ring bearer he  is tasked with carrying the one ring  back to mount doom  and casting it into