ing these years  the retired adventurer doesn't remain  idle along with helping to restore his  home he spends a period of time serving  as the interim mayor of michel delving  capital of the shire he also spends a  great deal of time working on the red  book of westmarch this famous tome was  begun by bilbo who used it to record  among  other things the story of his own  adventures frodo organizes a manuscript  and then adds his own accounts of the  war of the ring he gives the book an  appropriately epic title the downfall of  the lord of the rings and the return of  the king  while frodo is the primary author of the  red book his friends sam  pippin and mary add to it in various  ways  exhausted and worn down frodo finally  makes the hard decision to leave middle  earth after the war of the ring  arwen even star daughter of the great  elf elrond  now the queen of gondor chooses to  become mortal and stay with her husband  aragorn her ability to make this  sacrifice stems from her grandfather's  efforts  to save the world as chronicled in the  silmarillion arwyn's mortality means she  can no longer travel to the west with  the rest of the elves she gives frodo  her spot as a passenger and one of the  ships that will take him to the blessed  realm  a sort of heaven on earth for the  immortal beings few mortals are allowed  to make this trip  but given their roles in the destruction  of the one ring both bilbo and frodo are  awarded the special  privilege and so frodo leaves his  friends and middle earth behind  tolkien doesn't provide any more clues  about what frodo's life is like on the  other side of the water  instead he leaves us with a single  tantalizing line near the end of the  return of the king  and then it seems to him that the grey  rain curtain turned all to silver glass  and was rolled back and he beheld white  shores and beyond them a far green  country  under a swift sunrise check out one of  our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about the  lord of the rings are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

